        "title": "Why turns lose people their balance",
        "content": "During a turn the base temporarily shrinks to the pivot foot, so the center has very little room to wander. If the body rises, leans or swings wide mid-turn, the center leaves that small base and the turn becomes a stumble. Controlled turns keep everything stacked over the pivot until the second foot plants."
